# Arquitetura Java

Seguir `specs/backend/architecture/overview.md`.

## Camadas

- `domain` — só modelos/enums/exceptions; sem Spring/JPA/Kafka
- `application` — use cases e ports; orquestra domínio
- `infrastructure` — adapters que implementam ports
- `interfaces` — REST DTOs/controllers/filters

## Exemplos

```java
// ❌ BAD — regra no controller
@PostMapping
public ResponseEntity<?> transfer(@RequestBody req) {
  if (user.getBalance().compareTo(amount) < 0) return badRequest();
}

// ✅ GOOD — controller delega ao use case
@PostMapping
public ResponseEntity<TransactionResponse> transfer(@Valid @RequestBody TransferRequest req) {
  return created(mapper.toResponse(transferUseCase.execute(...)));
}
```

- Novas regras → `BR-XXX` em `specs/backend/product/business-rules.md` + teste
